  "subtitle": "The office mail cart that chased you down a chemical trail and gave you thirty seconds to grab your mail",
  "why_scout_cares": "A 600-pound autonomous mail robot that navigated offices by following an invisible ultraviolet-fluorescent chemical trail, then stopped at each desk, beeped and flashed, and gave secretaries a hard thirty-second window to grab their mail from locked shelves before it rolled on. Embodied, deadline-driven, commercially deployed (Sears Tower was its first building; the FBI ran one), and utterly unlike any input device in the museum — the interaction is a physical choreography between humans and a moving machine.",
